module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.Relative

/-!
# The classifying morphism of a trivialized invertible degree-one quotient

`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.F3.ProjF1Dehomogenization.Basic` turns a quotient pair together
with a trivialization datum into a ring homomorphism out of the graded ring of homogeneous
sections over an affine open of the base, and
`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.F3.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.Relative` turns such a homomorphism into
a morphism into relative `Proj` over that open, provided it inverts one positive-degree
homogeneous section. This file composes the two, which is the local half of Tag 01NA's
"`X = U₁`" and hence of Tag 01O4's classifying morphism.

The section inverted is a degree-one one, as the source's generation hypothesis dictates: a pair
`(ℒ, ψ)` has `ℒ` generated by the images `ψ(s)` of the degree-one sections `s`, so on the open
where one such image is a basis the corresponding coefficient is a unit — and that is exactly
the hypothesis `hu` below.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.fromOfPair`: the morphism to the absolute
  `Proj` of the graded ring of sections over an affine open of the base, classified by a
  quotient pair whose degree-one coefficient at a chosen homogeneous section is a unit.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.toRelativeProjOfPair`: the corresponding
  morphism into relative `Proj`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.fromOfPair_preimage_basicOpen`: the morphism
  lands in the standard open of the inverted section, so it is in the domain of the chart
  bijection `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.chartHomEquiv` and is therefore the
  unique morphism inducing its own homomorphism out of the `Away` ring.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.fromOfPair_toSpecZero`: its composite to
  `Spec` of the degree-zero part is the one determined by the dehomogenization.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.toRelativeProjOfPair_comp_toBase`: the
  morphism into relative `Proj` lies over the affine open it was built on.

## Implementation notes

**The covering family is already in the library and is not restated here.** That the standard opens of
the degree-one homogeneous elements cover an absolute `Proj` of a ring generated in degree one
is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.iSup_basicOpen_degreeOne_eq_top`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjRepresentsF1/TwistPowers.lean`), instantiated at
`A.grading U` by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` applied to
an affine open. The implementation notes of
`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.F3.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.Relative` list that covering as part of
the residue of the label; it is the result cited above, and nothing here
needs to re-derive it.

**The target scheme is arbitrary.** `fromOfPair` is stated for any scheme `X` carrying a
trivialization datum valued in `Γ(X, ⊤)`, not only for an open subscheme of the test scheme
`T`. That is the shape the glueing step consumes — it is applied to the members of a cover of
`T` — and it costs nothing, since `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` is itself stated
for an arbitrary scheme.

## What is not done here

No project tag is attached, and no bijection is constructed. The trivialization datum `Θ` is a
hypothesis here, and it is constructed for the fourth assertion of the label `01O4 "represents_f1"` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.Trivialization` —
`datumOfTrivialization`, from a morphism `g : X ⟶ T`, a trivialization of `g^*ℒ` and a ring
homomorphism out of `Γ(X, g⁻¹f⁻¹U)`, with `datumOfTrivialization_pairPieceHom_one` computing the
coefficient that `hu` asks to be a unit. What the label still needs beyond this file is
therefore: the cover of the test scheme by opens carrying such a trivialization on which some
degree-one image is a basis of `ℒ`; the glueing of these local morphisms along it; and the
bijectivity of the assembled map on strict-equivalence classes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization

universe u

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S) (TA : TensorAlgebras.{u})
  {T : Scheme.{u}} {f : T ⟶ S} (P : F1Pair A TA f) (U : S.Opens) {X : Scheme.{u}}
  (Θ : GradedSectionAlgebraHom (TA T P.L).tensor (op (f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) Γ(X, ⊤))
  {s : A.sectionPieces U 1}

/-- **The morphism to the absolute `Proj` classified by a trivialized quotient pair.** The
dehomogenization of the pair inverts the degree-one homogeneous section `s` by hypothesis, so
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.fromOfIsUnit` applies. -/
public def fromOfPair (hu : IsUnit (pairPieceHom A TA P U Θ 1 s)) :
    X ⟶ Proj (A.grading U) :=
  ProjF1DegreeOneChart.fromOfIsUnit (A.grading U) (dehomogenize A TA P U Θ) Nat.one_pos
    (A.of_mem_grading U s) (by
      refine (dehomogenize_of A TA P U Θ s).symm ▸ hu)

/-- **The classified morphism lands in the standard open of the inverted section.** So it is an
element of the domain of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1DegreeOneChart.chartHomEquiv`, hence
the unique morphism to `Proj` inducing its own homomorphism out of the `Away` ring at `s`. -/
public theorem fromOfPair_preimage_basicOpen (hu : IsUnit (pairPieceHom A TA P U Θ 1 s)) :
    fromOfPair A TA P U Θ hu ⁻¹ᵁ
        Proj.basicOpen (A.grading U) (DirectSum.of (A.sectionPieces U) 1 s) = ⊤ :=
  ProjF1DegreeOneChart.fromOfIsUnit_preimage_basicOpen (A.grading U) (dehomogenize A TA P U Θ)
    Nat.one_pos (A.of_mem_grading U s) _

/-- **The composite to `Spec` of the degree-zero part is the dehomogenization's own.** This is
Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections_toSpecZero` read at the classified
morphism; with `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization.dehomogenize_strHom` it says the
degree-zero data of the pair is what places the morphism over the base. -/
public theorem fromOfPair_toSpecZero (hu : IsUnit (pairPieceHom A TA P U Θ 1 s)) :
    fromOfPair A TA P U Θ hu ≫ Proj.toSpecZero (A.grading U) =
      X.toSpecΓ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        ((dehomogenize A TA P U Θ).comp (algebraMap (A.grading U 0) (A.sectionRing U)))) :=
  Proj.fromOfGlobalSections_toSpecZero (A.grading U) (dehomogenize A TA P U Θ) _

/-- **The morphism into relative `Proj` classified by a trivialized quotient pair.** The chart
of relative `Proj` over an affine open of the base is the absolute `Proj` of the graded ring of
sections there, so the morphism of `fromOfPair` composes into relative `Proj`. -/
public def toRelativeProjOfPair (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hu : IsUnit (pairPieceHom A TA P U Θ 1 s)) :
    X ⟶ (relativeProj A).scheme :=
  ProjF1DegreeOneChart.toRelativeProjOfIsUnit A U hU (dehomogenize A TA P U Θ) Nat.one_pos
    (A.of_mem_grading U s) ((dehomogenize_of A TA P U Θ s).symm ▸ hu)

/-- **The morphism into relative `Proj` lies over the affine open it was built on**, which is
what makes it a point of Tag 01O4's functor over the base. -/
public theorem toRelativeProjOfPair_comp_toBase (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hu : IsUnit (pairPieceHom A TA P U Θ 1 s)) :
    toRelativeProjOfPair A TA P U Θ hU hu ≫ (relativeProj A).toBase =
      fromOfPair A TA P U Θ hu ≫ projInclusionToOpen A U hU ≫ U.ι :=
  ProjF1DegreeOneChart.toRelativeProjOfIsUnit_comp_toBase A U hU (dehomogenize A TA P U Θ)
    Nat.one_pos (A.of_mem_grading U s) _

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjF1Dehomogenization

end
